 ## Developer Setup
 
+### Private Unity packages
+
+The project reads `dev.world.sdk` and `gg.argus.rampage.gameplay` from private
+GitHub repositories. Let GitHub CLI configure a credential helper; keep tokens
+out of Git URLs and `Packages/manifest.json`:
+
+```bash
+gh auth login --git-protocol https --web
+gh auth setup-git --hostname github.com
+```
+
+Authorize the account for both repositories. CI uses separate fine-grained
+`MONOREPO_PAT` and `RAMPAGE_BACKEND_PAT` secrets with read-only Contents
+access; the auth action forwards scoped config into GameCI without changing
+package files. Secret-bearing Unity PR jobs run only for trusted same-repository
+contributors.
+
+For live shared-gameplay edits, open Unity Package Manager and choose **+ →
+Install package from disk**, then select the sibling backend checkout's
+`native/gameplay/Rampage.Gameplay/package.json`. Restore the tracked Git URL
+with **Install package from git URL** before committing; commit the UPM-updated
+manifest and lock together.
+
 ### [For Windows] Install WSL2
 
 It is recommended to always use WSL2 when interacting with the projects through CLI for consistency across all platforms.
